{"game": "warframe", "language": "english", "appid": 230410, "month": "2016-03", "window": 3, "start_date": 1458086400, "end_date": 1458777599, "month_true_total": 1347, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-14 18:54:12 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "22013567", "author": {"steamid": "76561198018860952", "personaname": "MultiDarkZen", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/29019/", "num_games_owned": 1444, "num_reviews": 198, "playtime_forever": 144289, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 129760, "deck_playtime_at_review": 20, "last_played": 1788065009, "avatar": "7372cb1ff09f98fb8ece824006fff6b475228b58"}, "language": "english", "review": "Warframe is one of those rare games where you can take a 5 year break and come back and its like nothing much has changed,  It's stayed so consistently great that I've been playing it on and off since 2014. I am a veteran player of the game, I have collected nearly almost all weapons and prime frames since since they released new ones, and I farm for a lot of the stuff I have this game took a decade worth of child hood since I played this game while in the hospital so its been a great time killer and I would play it on my old laptop at the time. Now I have a real gaming computer and a steam deck to play it on which I wish existed when I stuck in the hospital and now that its on phone as well the game has become even more portable. Though playing this game on the phone is kind of a nightmare due to the screen being cluttered with menus and the mobile controls aren't that great. Warframe is incredibly optimized and can run on pretty much anything these days.", "timestamp_created": 1458774615, "timestamp_updated": 1772386718, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam